{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "SHARED PUBLIC LIST. The genes of the ACMG SF v3.3 secondary findings — the minimum where the medical community holds an incidental pathogenic variant in a healthy person to be a reason to act. Nobody's genotypes are kept here.",
    "version": "ACMG SF v3.3",
    "published": "2025-06-23, Genetics in Medicine (policy statement ACMG), DOI 10.1016/j.gim.2025.101454, PMID 40568962",
    "gene_count": 84,
    "new_in_v33": [
      "ABCD1",
      "CYP27A1",
      "PLN"
    ],
    "removed_in_v33": [],
    "considered_not_added": [
      "GCK",
      "RUNX1",
      "SLC4A1",
      "ADA2 (decision deferred)"
    ],
    "report_rules": {
      "any": "report on a single pathogenic / likely pathogenic variant",
      "biallelic": "report only on TWO P/LP variants (recessive inheritance). One variant = carriership, not disease",
      "hfe_c282y_hom": "report only the p.C282Y homozygote. A heterozygote and H63D are not a secondary finding"
    },
    "provenance": "The full text of the paper in Genetics in Medicine is not directly available (403). The list was assembled by cross-checking several independent sources that reproduce the ACMG table: the official ACMG press release (acmg.net), the full v3.3 table from Ambry Genetics, Baylor Genetics, 3billion.io; inheritance modes and phenotypes for the 81 genes of v3.2 come from the official table on PMC/NIH (PMC10524344). The arithmetic adds up: 81 (v3.2) + 3 = 84.",
    "caveats": "The inheritance mode of the three new genes (ABCD1 XL, CYP27A1 AR, PLN AD) is taken from accepted clinical genetics rather than verbatim from the v3.3 table — verify it once the primary source becomes accessible. The category of RPE65 is «metabolic» in some sources and «other» in others — the majority reading was taken. In the official table LDLR is marked semidominant (SD) rather than plain AD: homozygotes and compound heterozygotes are affected more severely.",
    "how_to_use": "The list sets the FRAME of reporting, not a diagnosis. A finding in an SF gene is a reason to consult a geneticist and to check it clinically, not a conclusion that there is disease: see penetrance.json on why «pathogenic» != «will fall ill»."
  },
